{"assets":["/editorial-assets/1c0a6198b0cb77694db4c22ffbf5cf6f3f44d4ab4d615e40af20ef0ab8ff1dd4.png","/editorial-assets/7a186a7fa2ff36fdfd93c2a018f2bc5ee536ffc8667d267f04d24d3d65154b6d.png","/editorial-assets/e01cab18b2ad4e3a130c911c56c509bbb0c4aeae9d6151e7ff737249fa7a284c.png","/editorial-assets/0225bafae98ea4e3389bc46a790418789f589daa13cfaf566f8a53d080bc8626.png","/editorial-assets/111ecb061b8dc3e985df2a3f17bc84bf67f2f659806c9076542a90b592888db8.png","/editorial-assets/4ef60ea68c9579539cb097f618c9ab6506ea3d244e90030121287a804aa700a9.png","/editorial-assets/9d4899292163e02e9c48064212f06f7992558075327cf53ab0adc4f02e5e2070.png","/editorial-assets/438cb0dd69af0ff0526a230b3d2ea2cb1d7e2827cb04dc095fe66b2b6ec3386c.png","/editorial-assets/f228ae68ca502473f9c354eb5c11bca2fb227ef75ebfe569de2fcf3f3dc65a63.png","/editorial-assets/c59285aa5e25a7a09576c4a2f9024f7d080ae8bbaa7db94e58c0953a8fd5da29.png","/editorial-assets/030572163762f1662394629ee7a5536f9c6ec8837dff17ac9c20800225a01295.png","/editorial-assets/407eeceec4820eff9ab27a4e41fd1ecdb5b1f45882b43c02465e6dbe2f5faf04.png","/editorial-assets/0ab2096e6566bde9bf1a516fddd1d6d2dbfa4961cccffd8c2c37cee5384979e0.png","/editorial-assets/69c6688ff2071f106392678baab95e8ebeedd96b33000043929b322911b22dcc.png","/editorial-assets/05c047f470aaff7bb26b0be21a213c3e5fec0d653bef59bd98de5cb17c9181ea.png","/editorial-assets/c94142da1114add5dd933e7165b6691459bfa03f3b03b3ca91d01eada133fb19.png","/editorial-assets/cc35fb70e775b2b50fd21cab6b83058a2fc697ea6b2c2cd2baae163e3fa0475b.png","/editorial-assets/776edbb14aa2879b5d8106dfd3763f68935da95dd373074b5e51a9ae635a4468.png","/editorial-assets/b8697d79ee969535e705b98d1aa5ad418ecd3db7b8cc8913cfc0c48b52b274dc.png","/editorial-assets/d80f5f6670419869653e5adcad2ef628cc2fee9f8cbc907997ecc2ac64de152f.png","/editorial-assets/3dc323a1b0658a696d2a3a8bc9b952a2ceb529e120142dde22e93ab50ed0ac68.png"],"contestId":"621","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/621/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"621A - Wet Shark and Odd and Even"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First, if the sum of all the numbers is already even, then we do nothing. Otherwise, we remove the smallest odd number. Since, if the sum is odd, we need to remove a number with the same parity to make the sum even. Notice it's always bad to remove more odd numbers, and it does nothing to remove even numbers. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/621/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"621B - Wet Shark and Bishops"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's start with two bishops (x1, y1) and (x2, y2). Notice that if (x1, y1) attacks (x2, y2), either x1 + y1 == x2 + y2 OR x1 — y1 == x2 — y2. So, for each bishop (x, y), we will store x + y in one map and x — y in another map."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/621/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"621C - Wet Shark and Flowers"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") be the probability that the product of the number of flowers of sharks "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/1c0a6198b0cb77694db4c22ffbf5cf6f3f44d4ab4d615e40af20ef0ab8ff1dd4.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We want the expected value of the number of pairs of neighbouring sharks whose flower numbers are divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". From linearity of expectation, this is equal to the probabilities that each pair multiplies to a number divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(0) + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1) + ... + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). (Don't forget about the wrap-around at "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now, for each pair of neighbouring sharks, we need to figure out the probability that their product is divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Consider an interval ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"]. How many numbers in this interval are divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"? Well, it is easier if we break the interval ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"] up into [1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"] - [1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1]. Since 1, 2, ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" contains "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/7a186a7fa2ff36fdfd93c2a018f2bc5ee536ffc8667d267f04d24d3d65154b6d.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", the interval ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"] contains "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/e01cab18b2ad4e3a130c911c56c509bbb0c4aeae9d6151e7ff737249fa7a284c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now, consider two numbers "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0225bafae98ea4e3389bc46a790418789f589daa13cfaf566f8a53d080bc8626.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/111ecb061b8dc3e985df2a3f17bc84bf67f2f659806c9076542a90b592888db8.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", with "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/4ef60ea68c9579539cb097f618c9ab6506ea3d244e90030121287a804aa700a9.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the number of integers divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the interval ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"], and define "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" similarly. Now what's the probability that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"? We can count the opposite: the probability that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Since "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a prime, this means neither "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" nor "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". The number of integers in ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"] not divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". Similar for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Therefore, the probability "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not divisible by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is given by "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/9d4899292163e02e9c48064212f06f7992558075327cf53ab0adc4f02e5e2070.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Therefore, the probability it is can be given by "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/438cb0dd69af0ff0526a230b3d2ea2cb1d7e2827cb04dc095fe66b2b6ec3386c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Now, just sum over this for all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/621/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"621D - Rat Kwesh and Cheese"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The tricky Rat Kwesh has finally made an appearance; it is time to prepare for some tricks. But truly, we didn't expect it to be so hard for competitors though. Especially the part about taking log of a negative number."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We need a way to deal with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yz"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". We cannot directly compare them, 200"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"200"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"200"}],"kind":"superscript"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is way too big. So what we do? Take log! "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f228ae68ca502473f9c354eb5c11bca2fb227ef75ebfe569de2fcf3f3dc65a63.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is an increasing function on positive numbers (we can see this by taking "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/c59285aa5e25a7a09576c4a2f9024f7d080ae8bbaa7db94e58c0953a8fd5da29.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", then "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/030572163762f1662394629ee7a5536f9c6ec8837dff17ac9c20800225a01295.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", which is positive when we are dealing with positive numbers). So if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/407eeceec4820eff9ab27a4e41fd1ecdb5b1f45882b43c02465e6dbe2f5faf04.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When we take log, "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0ab2096e6566bde9bf1a516fddd1d6d2dbfa4961cccffd8c2c37cee5384979e0.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" But "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" can still be 200"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"200"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", which is still far too big. So now what can we do? Another log! But is it legal? When "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 0.1 for example, "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/69c6688ff2071f106392678baab95e8ebeedd96b33000043929b322911b22dcc.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", so we cannot take another log. When can we take another log, however? We need "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/05c047f470aaff7bb26b0be21a213c3e5fec0d653bef59bd98de5cb17c9181ea.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" to be a positive number. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" will always be positive, so all we need is for "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/c94142da1114add5dd933e7165b6691459bfa03f3b03b3ca91d01eada133fb19.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" to be positive. This happens when "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > 1. So if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > 1, everything will be ok. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is another good observation to make. If one of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is greater than 1, then we can always achieve some expression (out of those 12) whose value is greater than 1. But if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < 1, then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" will never be greater than 1. So if at least one of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is greater than 1, then we can discard those bases that are less than or equal to 1. In this case, "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/cc35fb70e775b2b50fd21cab6b83058a2fc697ea6b2c2cd2baae163e3fa0475b.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Remember that "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/776edbb14aa2879b5d8106dfd3763f68935da95dd373074b5e51a9ae635a4468.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", so "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/b8697d79ee969535e705b98d1aa5ad418ecd3db7b8cc8913cfc0c48b52b274dc.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Similarly, "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/d80f5f6670419869653e5adcad2ef628cc2fee9f8cbc907997ecc2ac64de152f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The last case is when "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 1. Then, notice that for example, "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/3dc323a1b0658a696d2a3a8bc9b952a2ceb529e120142dde22e93ab50ed0ac68.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". But the denominator of this fraction is something we recognize, because 10 / 3 > 1. So if all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < 1, then it is the same as the original problem, except we are looking for the minimum this time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/621/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"621E - Wet Shark and Blocks"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First, let us build an X by X matrix. We will be applying matrix exponentiation on this matrix. For each modulo value T from 0 to X — 1, and each value in the array with index i between 1 and n, we will do: matrix[T][(10 * T + arr[i]) % X]++. This is because, notice that for each block we allow one more way to go between a modulo value T, and (10 * T + arr[i]) % X. We are multiplying T by 10 because we are \"left-shifting\" the number in a way (i.e. changing 123 -> 1230), and then adding arr[i] to it. Notice that this basically simulates the concatenation that Wet Shark is conducting, without need of a brute force dp approach. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/23196"}